{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 30747.7, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "precision-recall-or-fresh-domain", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "Continued Think Free project: investigated view-count principle on GitHub code repositories. Designed and ran fresh observation experiment (E203) testing whether the view-count principle generalizes to GitHub code repositories using star counts as arrival metric and GitHub topics for need classification. Experiment resulted in 3/4 gates passing with large effect size (3.99-6.08× median star count difference for need-related vs general repos). Created prototype command-line script (PROTOTYPE-viewcount-github-topic/) that implements topic-based classification and gate evaluation. Updated STATE-next-actions.md with E203 experiment entry and updated next action. Experiment result recorded in EXPERIMENTS/E203-github-repos-viewcount-*/RESULT.md. Key finding: view-count principle, previously validated on PyPI, NPM, NuGet, Discourse, and Stack Exchange, now also generalizes to GitHub code repositories. No candidate validated across 7+ report domains; principle is a measurement methodology, not a product seed. Next action: precision/recall against hand-read repo labels, or move to fresh domain per D083.", "unlogged_changes": 54}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 81, "session": "2026-10-20-001-land-the-two-diverged-lineages-then-run", "ts": "2026-10-20T20:23:31+00:00"}
